            "Download from LoTW…",
            "Downloads the log from the ARRL Logbook of the World site with username and password (saved in the settings).",
            "The same EME budget as an Excel sheet: the green cells can be edited and the results update at once.",
            "MNR (Maximum Non-Reciprocity). With linearly polarised antennas the EME signal undergoes two rotations of the polarisation plane: the geometric one (Dpol), because the two stations see the Moon from different points of the Earth, and the Faraday rotation in the ionosphere, which depends on the Earth's magnetic field and on the state of the ionosphere and cannot be predicted.",
            "The Faraday rotation has the same sense in both directions of the path, while the geometric rotation is reversed: this is why the total angle can be different going from you to the DX and from the DX to you. The path becomes non-reciprocal: one of the two hears well and the other badly.",
            "MNR = -20·log|cos(2·Dpol)| is the worst case of this difference, in dB. With MNR 0 dB the two directions are always equal; with a high MNR (Dpol near ±45°) it can happen that you hear the DX and he does not hear you, or the opposite, even with identical stations. It is better to choose times with low MNR, or to use antennas with adjustable or circular polarisation.",
            "CFOM = Constant Frequency On the Moon. The motion of the Moon and the rotation of the Earth shift the frequency by the Doppler effect, differently for each station and changing with time (at 144 MHz up to about ±400 Hz one way, twice that for your own echo).",
            "With the CFOM method each station corrects only its own Doppler: it transmits on f0 - Doppler (so the signal reaches the Moon exactly at f0) and receives on f0 + Doppler. If both stations do this they always meet on the frequency f0 \"on the Moon\", without knowing the other's Doppler: it is as if the Moon were a fixed repeater on f0.",
            "In the program f0 is the set frequency (MHz + kHz); the TX me CFOM and RX me CFOM columns and the values on the main screen give the frequencies to set on the radio. WSJT-X uses the same scheme with Doppler tracking in \"Constant frequency on Moon\" mode.",
            "beta 19 - Title with the user's callsign; no default locator or callsign; settings in the program folder; new tab order; INSTRUCTIONS with all the parameters, MNR and CFOM; experimental-EXCEL tab; log download from LoTW; ABOUT & CREDITS; Hindi, Korean and Indonesian languages.",
            "With \"Download from LoTW…\" the log is downloaded directly from LoTW (username and password are asked for and saved in the settings).",
            "This guide: what the tabs are for, what each parameter means, MNR and CFOM, advice.",
            "EDITABLE PARAMETERS: WHAT THEY ARE AND WHAT THEY MEAN",
            "MNR AND CFOM: WHAT THEY MEAN",
            "With a 10-character locator the ground height is taken automatically from the web (Open Topo Data, Open-Meteo).",
