            "Height from the web not available for ",
            "Ground height for {0} from the web: {1:F0} m a.s.l. ({2}).",
            "Ground height from the 10-character locator",
            "Open Topo Data (EU-DEM 25 m in Europe, SRTM 30 m in the rest of the world) and, as an alternative, the Open-Meteo Elevation API (Copernicus DEM GLO-90, 90 m). OpenStreetMap does not provide height data and the Google Maps APIs require a paid key: that is why these free services are used.",
            "beta 20 - Ground height taken automatically from the web (Open Topo Data, Open-Meteo) when the locator has 10 characters.",
            "• Station height: with a 10-character locator the ground height is taken automatically from the web (Open Topo Data, Open-Meteo); with shorter locators enter it by hand. It is the ground height at the locator point, not the height of the antenna above the ground.",
